ging QA out to ten Sonnet sub-agents and four GPT testers over two days. This is what it cost, what it shipped, and where the money went.",[249,250,251,252],"$147.09 API-equivalent","58 findings, 65 commits","92% saved by caching","20 min median fix",[254,255,43],"agents","cost","\u003C!-- The report itself is public/reports/sub-agent-fanning/index.html (self-contained HTML from the /report skill).\n     Source: ~/dev/experiments/sub-agent-fanning. Review for internal details before deploying (see docs/bio.md §8). -->","content/reports/sub-agent-fanning.md","fdac1073bf2f95b7",{"html":256,"metadata":260},{"headings":261,"localImagePaths":262,"remoteImagePaths":263,"frontmatter":264,"imagePaths":268},[],[],[],{"title":242,"date":265,"kind":244,"model":245,"readingTime":246,"summary":247,"highlights":266,"tags":267},["Date","2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"],[249,250,251,252],[254,255,43],[],"puck-orchestration",{"id":269,"data":271,"body":284,"filePath":285,"digest":286,"rendered":287},{"title":272,"date":273,"kind":274,"model":245,"readingTime":275,"summary":276,"highlights":277,"tags":282,"published":31},"Revise the loop: the Claude weekly limit, not the 5-hour one, sets the Puck builder's pace",["Date","2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"],"Findings + replay","19 min read","A Fable 5.1 orchestrator ran Opus and Sonnet builders and two GPT-6 reviewers overnight on DagangNow's Puck store builder, and merged 3 of 31 tasks. A replay of the night, opening with a fan-out tree, shows where the tokens and the hours went: Claude and Codex never worked at the same time.",[278,279,280,281],"3 of 31 tasks merged","2.21M Claude output tokens","0 min builder/reviewer overlap","2-min replay + fan-out tree",[254,283,43],"orchestration","\u003C!-- The report is public/reports/puck-orchestration/index.html, built from docs/reports/puck-orchestration/body.html with the /report skill.\n     Videos are rendered from docs/reports/puck-orchestration/replay/. -->","content/reports/puck-orchestration.md","e7a5ab811096a275",{"html":284,"metadata":288},{"headings":289,"localImagePaths":290,"remoteImagePaths":291,"frontmatter":292,"imagePaths":296},[],[],[],{"title":272,"date":293,"kind":274,"model":245,"readingTime":275,"summary":276,"highlights":294,"tags":295},["Date","2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"],[278,279,280,281],[254,283,43],[],"gallery",["Map",299,300,320,321,340,341],"around-kl",{"id":299,"data":301,"filePath":310,"digest":311,"rendered":312},{"title":302,"place":303,"period":304,"summary":305,"order":30,"photos":306,"standIn":307},"Around KL","Kuala Lumpur","Ongoing","Walks with the A7R III, mostly after rain.",[],[308,309,308],"dusk","night","content/gallery/around-kl.md","8566ec196dbf7e62",{"html":35,"metadata":313},{"headings":314,"localImagePaths":315,"remoteImagePaths":316,"frontmatter":317,"imagePaths":319},[],[],[],{"title":302,"place":303,"period":304,"summary":305,"order":30,"standIn":318},[308,309,308],[],"studio-days",{"id":320,"data":322,"filePath":330,"digest":331,"rendered":332},{"title":323,"place":324,"period":325,"summary":326,"order":62,"photos":327,"standIn":328},"Studio days","SSC studio, UTM KL","University, year 2","Studio, cosplay and product shoots from the year I was the camera guy.",[],[329,329,309,329],"studio","content/gallery/studio-days.md","55d0fe247b828977",{"html":35,"metadata":333},{"headings":334,"localImagePaths":335,"remoteImagePaths":336,"frontmatter":337,"imagePaths":339},[],[],[],{"title":323,"place":324,"period":325,"summary":326,"order":62,"standIn":338},[329,329,309,329],[],"outdoors",{"id":340,"data":342,"filePath":350,"digest":351,"rendered":352},{"title":343,"place":344,"period":304,"summary":345,"order":227,"photos":346,"standIn":347},"Outdoors","Malaysia","Hills, coast, and whatever's on the way.",[],[348,349,348],"hills","sea","content/gallery/outdoors.md","9af8bd20d0d947b0",{"html":35,"metadata":353},{"headings":354,"localImagePaths":355,"remoteImagePaths":356,"frontmatter":357,"imagePaths":359},[],[],[],{"title":343,"place":344,"period":304,"summary":345,"order":227,"standIn":358},[348,349,348],[],"posts",["Map",362,363,377,378],"hello-world",{"id":362,"data":364,"body":374,"filePath":375,"digest":376,"deferredRender":31},{"title":365,"date":366,"description":367,"coverImageSrc":368,"tags":369,"published":31,"reports":373},"Add a Typed MDX Blog to Your Next.js Portfolio (Contentlayer)",["Date","2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"],"Turn your existing Next.js portfolio into a fast, SEO-friendly blog with Contentlayer and MDX.","./cover.png",[53,370,371,372,54],"MDX","Contentlayer","SEO",[],"Welcome to the blog! This is a seed post to verify listing, reading time, tags, and comments.\n\n## Why Contentlayer?\n\nContentlayer is a content SDK that transforms your content into type-safe JSON data. It works seamlessly with Next.js and provides:\n\n- **Type safety** - Full TypeScript support with auto-generated types\n- **MDX support** - Write content in MDX with custom components\n- **Computed fields** - Automatically calculate reading time, slugs, etc.\n- **Hot reload** - See changes instantly during development\n\n## Getting Started\n\nFirst, install the necessary dependencies:\n\n```bash\npnpm add contentlayer next-contentlayer reading-time\n```\n\nThen configure your content schema in `contentlayer.config.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nexport const Post = defineDocumentType(() => ({\n  name: \"Post\",\n  filePathPattern: `posts/**/*.mdx`,\n  contentType: \"mdx\",\n  fields: {\n    title: { type: \"string\", required: true },\n    date: { type: \"date\", required: true },\n    description: { type: \"string\", required: true },\n  },\n}));\n```\n\n## Features Included\n\nThis blog setup includes:\n\n1. **Auto reading time** - Calculated automatically from content\n2. **Tags with filter pages** - Navigate to `/blog/tag/[tag]` to filter\n3. **Giscus comments** - GitHub Discussions-powered comments\n4. **Full SEO** - Metadata, canonical URLs, sitemap, robots.txt, JSON-LD\n5. **Local search scaffold** - Simple search ready for enhancement\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Add more posts in `content/posts/`\n- Customize the MDX components\n- Set up Giscus for comments\n- Deploy and verify SEO\n\nHappy blogging! 🚀","content/posts/hello-world/index.mdx","31afc4df25d233cb","why-typescript",{"id":377,"data":379,"body":387,"filePath":388,"digest":389,"deferredRender":31},{"title":380,"date":381,"description":382,"coverImageSrc":368,"tags":383,"published":31,"reports":386},"Why TypeScript?",["Date","2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"],"My reasons for using TypeScript over JavaScript.",[384,385],"nextjs","typescript",[],"Throughout my journey in software engineering, I've struggled with choosing which language to even use.\n\n## Why TypeScript?\n\nHonestly, no particular reason — it's the language I use for most of my work. My first touch with frameworks was Next.js, so I dove right into TypeScript with barely any prior knowledge. Even when coming from JavaScript, I had a lot to learn.\n\nAfter using TypeScript for a while, I can see the benefits of it over JavaScript. From improved tooling to fewer runtime surprises. More thoughts to come — lemme deploy this first and write tomorrow.","content/posts/why-typescript/index.mdx","a96dc8cca3c3124a"]